Some <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18-pro/">iPhone 18 Pro</a> owners have noticed an unusual crackling sound coming from the speaker of the device, leading to complaints on <a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/iphone-18-pro-max-speaker-issue.2489836/">the <em>MacRumors</em> forums</a> and <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/iphone/comments/1wkrxv8/iphone_18pro_max_speaker_issue/">Reddit</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/Apple-iPhone-18-Pro-2up-16x9-1.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1063346" /><br/>
Users have called it a crackle, a faint tick or pop, or random clicking. Many say the problem is with the earpiece speaker, and both the &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj; and &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj; Max appear to be affected.<br/>
<br/>
Some people hear the sound consistently, while others hear it during app use, scrolling websites, when receiving notifications, when the keyboard pops up, or when making a call using a cellular connection. On affected units, reports suggest toggling Airplane Mode on and off triggers the sound, as does adjusting screen brightness quickly.<br/>
<br/>
Apple <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/28/apple-releases-ios-27-0-1/">released iOS 27.0.1</a> yesterday to fix a bug that could cause &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj; models to restart when <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/mask-face-id/">Face ID</a> authentication fails. The release notes didn't mention a speaker fix, and early feedback says the update <a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/iphone-18-pro-max-speaker-issue.2489836/page-2?post=34829814#post-34829814">did not help</a>.<br/>
<br/>
